  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given:<br /><br /><img height=\"93\" src=\"assets\\qt0045_dfe9caafc7e1.png\" width=\"410\" /><br /><br />On the basis of data given above, predict which of the following gases shows the least adsorption on a definite amount of charcoal?</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Method <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>:<br />The extent of adsorption is directly proportional to the critical temperature. As <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;has&nbsp;the lowest critical temperature, it will have the lowest extent of adsorption.<br /><br />Method <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>:<br />The value of adsorption is dependent on the intermolecular forces of attraction. Among the given options, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> will have the weakest van der Waal&#39;s force (London Dispersion), in which only <math><mn>2</mn></math> electrons are involved.<br /><br />Hence, as a force of attraction is the weakest for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></math> it will have the lowest adsorption value."
  }
}